The full changed-tests suite now passes: 297 pass, 0 fail, exit 0. The repair is committed as **`00c743c`**, a new commit on `b120086` (not an amendment), and `report-u1.md` has a new repair section.

**The bug:** `withAlteredFile` always used the same backup file name and never checked whether its copy, write or rename worked. A probe showed that once one Playground worker had renamed the backup away, another worker's `copy()` to that name failed with "No such file or directory". `file_exists()` still reported the backup as present. The edit was written anyway and the restore then failed, which matches the 2.4.2 bytes B saw. Each edit now uses a backup name with a random UUID, and every step is read back. The restored-byte assertion is unchanged.

Changed files and reasons:
- `test/plugin/version-fixtures.ts`: the shared, checked `withAlteredFile` (unique backup name, hash readback of the backup, the edit and the restore; restored-byte assertion kept).
- `test/plugin/compatibility.test.ts`: its local unchecked helper is replaced by a thin wrapper around the shared one that still writes the evidence note. All refusal assertions are unchanged.
- `test/plugin/harness.test.ts`: a new regression covering 7 repeated edits and 2 nested rounds, checking what every worker sees each time.
- No production code, pins or helper version changed. The temporary probe file is still deleted.

